# Vercel Performance Rules

## Data Fetching
- Use `next: { revalidate }` or `cache: 'force-cache'` for fetch
- Add `next: { tags }` for on-demand revalidation
- Never call `fetch` in middleware

## Images
- Use `next/image` with explicit `width` and `height`
- Prevents CLS; enables Vercel Image Optimization (AVIF, WebP)

## Animations
- Animate only `transform`, `opacity`
- Never animate `width`, `height`, `top`, `left`
- Never use `transition: all`

## Streaming
- Use Suspense for deferred data
- Show loading skeleton immediately; stream content
- Reduces TTFB and improves perceived performance
